  "title": "Cumulative Match Acceptances by Player",
  "prompt": "You are analyzing a multiplayer matchmaking system. The `match_invitations` table records every time a player is invited to join a match. Write a query that shows each invitation along with the player's cumulative number of accepted matches up to and including that invitation's timestamp. The output should include `player_id`, `invited_at`, `accepted` (whether this specific invitation was accepted), and `cumulative_acceptances` (the running total of accepted invitations for that player up to this point in time). Order the results by `player_id` ascending, then `invited_at` ascending. Note that some players may decline invitations (accepted = false), and these should still appear in the output but not increment the cumulative count.",
